# Local development secrets for `wrangler dev`.
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` and fill in the values. `.dev.vars` is
# git-ignored and must never be committed — the pre-commit hook refuses it.
#
# In PRODUCTION these are NOT read from a file. Set each one with
#   npx wrangler secret put <NAME>
# so it lives only in Cloudflare Secrets. See README.md → Deploy.
#
# Note: R2_ACCOUNT_ID is NOT here — it is a non-secret `var` in wrangler.jsonc,
# not a secret. Nor is the allow-list seed, for the same reason.
#
# Note: there is no account credential here either. Each person signs in at
# /authorize with their own Apple ID and their own Apple app-specific password,
# and that password lives only inside their own encrypted grant. The server
# holds no Apple identity of its own.

# HMAC key for calendar confirmation tokens (CALW-04). It signs and verifies
# those tokens and does nothing else, so rotating it invalidates every token in
# flight and breaks nothing else. Generate a fresh random value, e.g.
#   openssl rand -base64 32
CONFIRM_SECRET=

# R2 S3 API token for presigned attachment uploads. Create an R2 API token
# scoped to the attachments bucket with Object Read & Write only
# (Cloudflare dashboard → R2 → Manage API tokens). It yields these two halves.
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# The key that seals attachment save links (Phase 29.1). 32 random bytes,
# base64url with no padding. In production it is set from standard input and
# never printed. Leave it unset locally unless you are testing the save tool.
# SAVE_LINK_SEAL_KEY=
